{"source_slots":{"s4":"I'm thinking more of a weekend camping trip, maybe some hiking trails. I don't want to carry too much, but I still want to be prepared in case something goes wrong.","s5":"That sounds like a great plan! For a weekend camping trip on trails, you don't need a full survival kit, but having a couple of "must-haves" is key. For instance, a high-quality, lightweight multi-tool or a good small knife is your best friend, combined with a small first-aid kit for minor cuts or blisters.

Since you're on hiking trails, you could focus on "tool-as-snacks." For instance, instead of just bringing a bag of snacks, maybe you just focus on high-energy, lightweight snacks like trail mix, which serves both as a snack and a quick energy boost for the hike.

Do you have a specific type of terrain in mind—like dense forest, rocky mountains, or maybe just a simple woods hike? Knowing that will help determine if a specific lightweight tool is better than a heavy, full kit!"}}
